PAPER.md.cuts: where the new lines in PAPER.md and README.md come from.

PAPER.md was written by hand (d92caec): each result section copies its folder files word for word,
headings one level down. No generator; any content fix goes to the source file and to the copy.

Review fixes (11-18, after an outside review):
- "Some referenced evidence isn't included in this repository." <- given verbatim in the review
  brief. Replaces, in PAPER.md, "The folders also hold the referee and certificate code." and, in
  PAPER.md and README.md, "Each folder here holds the claim, the primary-source derivation, the
  referee's verdict, and the checker the referee wrote without the finder's code." (Coulomb and KITE
  have no checker code here; referee_certificate/VERIFIED.json is not in the repository.)
- Removed from PAPER.md and README.md: "Agents make the search cheap, so what matters is whether
  anyone else can rerun the check."
- "# ai-physics: the record" and "This file puts the record of every result" <- the same lines
  with "full" removed.
- KITE: the Verdicts section comes first; the bug list follows under "## Bugs: pre-referee report;
  final dispositions above" (heading from ai-biology PAPER.md, cc3c612).
- KITE: "The repro, evidence, dependency and upstream folders named below aren't bundled in this
  repository." <- new note for the KITE section; replaces nothing. Those links are kept as plain
  text in BUGS.md, VERDICTS.md and the copy.
- KITE BUGS.md: "# Confirmed KITE correctness bugs" -> "# KITE correctness bugs (four confirmed;
  CFG-002 excluded as intended behaviour)", and "These five bugs were not found" -> "These five
  reports were not found". Counting words only; matches README.md ("4 confirmed bugs", "judged
  intended behaviour") and VERDICTS.md (CFG-002 INTENDED).
- Private working paths were removed in the source folder files themselves, then in the copy:
  "a private working copy; only some of these files are in this repository", "a rented compute
  pod" / "the pod", "the pod helper script (not published)", "the local machine", "gh api".
  Reproduction blocks made only of private helper calls keep their step names and say the pod
  scripts aren't bundled.
- Link targets: PHYSICS.md's "the derivation" -> friends/vieira-stampedes-seed/coulomb-follow-up/
  DERIVATION.md and BUGS.md's combined.patch -> friends/ferreira-kite/combined.patch, in the copy
  only (the source links already resolve from their own folder).
- KITE BUGS.md Evidence lines: the folder each list came from is kept as plain text, e.g.
  "(`repro/KITE-CFG-001/`)", taken from the removed link targets.
